There are multiple ways to represent a graph in memory, but this book uses adjacency lists. In
this representation, each node has a collection of adjacent nodes (using std::vector). For an
unweighted graph, this adjacency list contains pointers to adjacent nodes. The graph is then
just a collection of such nodes:
struct GraphNode
